.TH SFCD 8 "" "Seafield Cluster" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sfcd \- Seafield Cluster node daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sfcd \-\-config
.I node.yaml
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sfcd
runs on every server of a Seafield Cluster. It keeps the cluster state with
Raft, talks to the other servers over SFCP and runs containers through
Seafield Engine
.RB ( sfed ),
which ships with it in
.IR /usr/lib/sfc/bin .
.PP
Commands: check (validate node.yaml and reach the engine), init (create a
cluster on this server), join (join an existing cluster), run (the
service), engine-config (write
.I /etc/sfe/daemon.json
from node.yaml). Run
.B sfcd \-\-help
for all of them.
.PP
The package installs the
.B sfcd.service
and
.B sfed.service
units without enabling them. After init or join:
.B systemctl enable \-\-now sfed sfcd
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sfc/node.yaml
the server's configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/sfc
cluster state and the server identity. Removing the package keeps it.
.TP
.I /run/sfcdp.sock
management socket for
.BR sfcli (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sfcli (1),
https://github.com/jay94ks/seafield/tree/main/docs
